INT. WHALE-BONE APOTHECARY - NIGHT

A shop built inside the ribcage of a dead leviathan. Ribs arch overhead like cathedral beams. Jars glow green on bone shelves.

SORREL VANE, 20s, apprentice, grinds something blue in a mortar. A cauldron simmers behind her.

The door swings open on a gust of salt air. No one is there. Sorrel looks up.

SORREL
Hello?

The jars hum. A drip falls from the roof of the ribcage. Another.

SORREL (CONT'D)
We're closed.

The bell above the door rings, by itself.

SORREL (CONT'D)
Show yourself.

A shape in the corner thickens. Flickers. Resolves.

OSWIN GRIST, ancient, barnacle-crusted, a drowned sailor in a coat of kelp, steps from the shadows. Water pours from his sleeves.

OSWIN
I need a remedy, girl.

SORREL
For what?

OSWIN
Breathing.

Sorrel sets down the mortar. The cauldron boils over.
